How to Prepare for an Unexpected Heavy Period

Sometimes your period can be heavier than expected. You may think your usual supplies are enough, only to discover that your flow has increased.

Having an emergency period plan can help you handle unexpected heavy-flow days.

Why Can Your Flow Feel Unexpected?

Menstrual flow can naturally vary from cycle to cycle. Changes in your usual pattern may also occur for various reasons.

Tracking your periods can help you recognise your typical flow and identify unusual changes.

Build a Period Emergency Kit

A useful emergency kit can include:

Extra sanitary pads
Spare underwear
Disposal bags
Tissues
Hand sanitiser
A small pouch for privacy

Keep one in your handbag, backpack, or workplace drawer.

Choose Protection According to Your Flow

If you know that certain days are usually heavier, carry sanitary pads that provide appropriate absorbency and coverage.

TIME Ultra Velvet can be part of your emergency period kit, giving you a comfortable menstrual protection option when your flow is heavier.

What If You Experience Leakage?

Don't panic. Find a washroom as soon as possible, change your pad, and use spare clothing if necessary.

Having backup supplies means an unexpected leak does not have to ruin your entire day.

Track Changes

If your period becomes unexpectedly heavy repeatedly, record the changes. Note how long the bleeding lasts and how frequently you need to change your pad.

If the change is significant or persistent, discuss it with a healthcare professional.

Conclusion

You cannot predict every change in your menstrual flow, but you can prepare for it.

Keep your period emergency kit ready and choose suitable menstrual protection.

